## ⬡ SONICRESUME GROUP: MASTER SOFTWARE SERVICES & LICENSING AGREEMENT
Corporate Framework Document | Operational Authority: Noah Workspace Ecosystem
This Master Agreement ("Agreement") is executed by and between SonicResume Group (herein "The Provider") and the purchasing entity or licensee (herein "The Client"). By purchasing source code, contracting cloud deployments, or commissioning custom app creations, both parties agree to the binding clauses outlined below.
------------------------------
## 📦 1. Intellectual Property & Source Code Licensing
The Provider grants licenses to its software repositories (including but not limited to Noah Resume, Noah Recruiter, Noah Image Studio, and Noah Vision Guard) under two strict operational frameworks:
## A. End-User License Agreement (EULA)

* Scope: Grants the Client non-exclusive, non-transferable access to utilize the compiled application layers hosted on the Provider's servers.
* Restrictions: The Client shall not inspect, copy, modify, or attempt to extract the underlying frontend scripts, database schemas, or API endpoints.

## B. Commercial Source Code Buyout License

* Scope: Grants the Client complete, perpetual, royalty-free intellectual property rights to the designated repository codebase.
* Privileges: The Client may alter, rebrand (white-label), host, duplicate, and resell the application as an independent service, keeping 100% of generated user fees.
* Exclusions: The Client shall not resell or distribute the raw, uncompiled repository source files as a developer asset template to other software engineers.

------------------------------
## ⚙️ 2. Cloud Infrastructure & Deployment Services
For custom deployment contracts where the Provider bridges codebases to the Client's private environment, the following structural parameters apply:

* Scope of Work: The Provider will securely sync target Git repositories, establish Vercel edge runtime networks, configure live Firebase database instances, and link secure Stripe transaction gateways.
* Client Obligations: The Client must provide valid administrative access tokens for their cloud accounts. The Client retains 100% financial responsibility for all ongoing hosting fees, data usage fees, and third-party API transaction processing fees.
* Handoff & Sign-off: Upon successful deployment showing a working web link, a 48-hour testing window begins. If no critical errors are logged within this window, the deployment is marked as completed and finalized.

------------------------------
## 🛠️ 3. Software Modifications & Engineering Bug Fixes
To maintain high software reliability across all custom workspace setups, debugging operations adhere to these parameters:

* Warranty Window: All paid source code buyouts and deployment services include a 30-day structural engineering warranty. The Provider will fix any local build crashes or deployment pipeline script breakages during this window at zero additional cost.
* Post-Warranty Debugging: Following the 30-day window, system maintenance, software dependency updates (e.g., Node.js or Vite version changes), and custom feature add-ons are billed separately.
* Exclusions: The Provider is not responsible for crashes caused by the Client modifying core structural code files, changing database schema fields, or deleting environment keys after final handoff.

------------------------------
## 💸 4. Unified Commercial Rate Sheet

| Service / Asset Class | Price (USD) | Payment Terms |
|---|---|---|
| Standard App User License | $99.00 – $499.00 | Paid upfront via Stripe (One-Time or Yearly) |
| Commercial Source Code Buyout | $1,500.00 – $4,500.00 | Paid upfront per codebase bundle |
| Standard Cloud Deployment Setup | $1,500.00 | Fixed rate per application deployment node |
| On-Premise / AI GPU Optimization | $2,500.00 | Fixed rate per server/WSL infrastructure setup |
| Custom App Creations & Retainers | $150.00 / Hour | 50% upfront deposit / 50% upon milestone delivery |

------------------------------
## 🔐 5. Liability, Security, & Absolute Indemnity

* Data Governance: The software architecture leverages serverless edge routines (Firebase/Stripe) to minimize system data tracking. The Provider is not liable for data privacy leaks resulting from weak client administration keys or poor password hygiene.
* No AI Cost Vulnerabilities: Because the core Noah Resume module operates reliably without AI dependency overhead, the Provider is entirely exempt from third-party AI platform outages, rate-limit locks, or token billing spikes on the client environment.
* Limitation of Liability: In no event shall SonicResume Group be held liable for any commercial losses, database downtime, or indirect financial damages exceeding the total amount paid by the Client for the specific service rendered.

